# CI x64 audit for DxUi native UIA lifetime candidate

Workflow run `36358394952` targets `49c963f5751a6754e6b08e0362b96cfc7fc64414`. The validation job and the x64 Debug, Release, and ASan Debug native jobs are complete and successful.

The downloaded x64 artifacts contain 62 successful suite receipts. Each is x64/X64, exit code 0, and has an empty skip list. Raw matching logs corroborate completion using each suite harness format: most end with `[DONE]` and `All DxUi tests passed.`, while Embedded, Foundation, and MenuExitLifetime use their suite-specific PASS/EXIT markers. Test executable SHA claims are internally consistent by executable path. Artifact downloads do not contain those executable files, so executable SHA values are cross-checked across receipts and linked performance reports, not recomputed from binaries.

External consumer receipts pass in Debug and Release with STL annotations enabled, and in ASan Debug with both annotation modes. Each reports 12 native-module checks and 10 negative checks. The ASan runtime probe deliberately exits 1, reports `detected:true`, and the corresponding log contains the expected heap-use-after-free diagnostic and `ABORTING`; it is an expected-detection check, not a suite failure.

The linked performance receipts identify the exact CI commit and report a clean source tree. Every reported benchmark-input SHA-256 matches the bytes in a clean checkout of that commit. The checkout is CRLF-normalized on Windows, so the check uses the exact consumer-visible checkout bytes rather than raw Git blob bytes. Source and binary inventories are in `source-hash-manifest.json` and `suite-audit.json`; every downloaded x64 artifact hash is in `x64-artifact-hashes.json`.

The workflow remains `in_progress` because ARM64 jobs have not completed. This audit therefore makes no full-matrix pass claim.

